## Where do the pages live?

Documentation is plain Markdown in `content/docs`. Folders create navigation groups. `_index.md` names a group and controls its order.

## How do I add a page?

Create a Markdown file with frontmatter:

```md
---
title: "Invite a teammate"
description: "Add someone to a workspace"
order: 2
---

## Invite a teammate

Write the shortest path to a successful result.
```

## Are these pages available to LLM tools?

Yes. `/llms.txt` lists the public documentation and every page has a raw `.md` version. Remove those routes if the product should not publish machine-readable docs.

## Can I replace these pages?

Yes. Replace these pages with real product documentation or remove the Docs module from the owned application code.
